`]}),e.jsxs(r,{title:"Tiles, matrix units and a pipeline",children:[e.jsxs(s.p,{children:["FlashAttention splits Q, K and V into tiles that fit in shared memory and computes ",e.jsx(s.code,{children:"QKᵀ"})," and the product of the probabilities with ",e.jsx(s.code,{children:"V"})," on Tensor Cores, the matrix units of Week 4, one in each sub-partition of slide 7. A kernel uses them through matrix multiply-accumulate (MMA) instructions, which a whole warp or a group of warps issues together. On Hopper the largest MMA instructions are issued by a warpgroup, four contiguous warps whose first warp's rank is a multiple of 4 ",e.jsx(i,{id:"nvidia2026ptx",children:"NVIDIA, 2026c"})," ",e.jsx(i,{id:"nvidia2022hopper",children:"Andersch et al., 2022"}),". The softmax kernel has no matrix product and uses no Tensor Cores."]}),e.jsxs(s.p,{children:["Data movement overlaps with this arithmetic. Hopper's Tensor Memory Accelerator (TMA), the unit below the sub-partitions on slide 7, copies large blocks between global and shared memory asynchronously ",e.jsx(i,{id:"nvidia2022hopper",children:"Andersch et al., 2022"}),", so the next K/V tile arrives while the current one is in use. With warp specialization, producer warps only issue copies, consumer warps only compute, and shared-memory buffers pass the tiles between them. The schedule and the data movement change, and the result is still exact attention."]})]})]}),e.jsxs(t,{title:"FlashAttention-4 rebalances the work for Blackwell",accent:6,number:"29",children:[e.jsxs(s.table,{children:[e.jsx(s.thead,{children:e.jsxs(s.tr,{children:[e.jsx(s.th,{children:"Per SM, per clock"}),e.jsx(s.th,{style:{textAlign:"right"},children:"Hopper"}),e.jsx(s.th,{style:{textAlign:"right"},children:"Blackwell B200"})]})}),e.jsxs(s.tbody,{children:[e.jsxs(s.tr,{children:[e.jsx(s.td,{children:"bf16 MMA operations"}),e.jsx(s.td,{style:{textAlign:"right"},children:"4,096"}),e.jsx(s.td,{style:{textAlign:"right"},children:"8,192"})]}),e.jsxs(s.tr,{children:[e.jsx(s.td,{children:"Exponentials"}),e.jsx(s.td,{style:{textAlign:"right"},children:"16"}),e.jsx(s.td,{style:{textAlign:"right"},children:"16"})]}),e.jsxs(s.tr,{children:[e.jsx(s.td,{children:"Shared memory bytes"}),e.jsx(s.td,{style:{textAlign:"right"},children:"128"}),e.jsx(s.td,{style:{textAlign:"right"},children:"128"})]})]})]}),e.jsxs(s.ul,{children:[`
